  "slug": "inference-fit-6a61",
  "summary": "Euclid, Rubin, SPHEREx and SKA-era pipelines are being benchmarked and automated, with SDC3b exposing inter-team variability in EoR inference.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the construction and validation of inference components for Euclid, Rubin, SPHEREx and SKA-era data. Self-supervised models are applied to imaging: EuclidFM learns 128-dim source embeddings from Euclid Q1 photometry, and JAISP fuses ten-band Rubin and Euclid imaging for detection and astrometry. Lens-Orchestra uses multimodal LLM agents to automate forward modeling of 185 Euclid Q1 lens candidates. On the systematics and emulation side, SPHEREx clustering uses information-criterion-driven non-linear deprojection tested on lognormal mocks, symbolic regression diagnoses a Lyman-alpha GP emulator, and a differentiable GPU-accelerated forward model targets 21-cm uncertainty quantification. SDC3b reports inter-team variability among 16 EoR pipelines, underscoring the need for cross-method validation. The items span different observables and methods.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
